---
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code as CodeSnippet } from "astro:components";
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/ap-csp/" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back
        </a>

        <h1>Section Summary: Iteration</h1>
        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-4" />

        <p class="text-secondary">
          Activities 1.17 &ndash; 1.22. Use this to review, or to fill in a definition you missed.
        </p>

        <hr />

        <section>
          <h2><span class="text-sn-theme">1.</span> Repeating With while</h2>

          <p>
            A loop needs three things: a variable
            to start from, a condition to keep going, and a change that
            eventually makes the condition false.
          </p>

          <dl>
            <dt>Iteration</dt>
            <dd>Repeating a block of code.</dd>
            <dt>Loop body</dt>
            <dd>The statements inside the loop's braces.</dd>
            <dt>Infinite loop</dt>
            <dd>A loop whose condition never becomes false.</dd>
            <dt>Accumulator</dt>
            <dd>
            A variable that collects a running result across passes of a
            loop.
            </dd>
          </dl>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section>
          <h2><span class="text-sn-theme">2.</span> p5 Lab 4: The Loop You Didn't Write</h2>

          <p>
            The lab's{" "}
            <CodeSnippet code="draw()" lang={"javascript"} theme={"material-theme-ocean"} inline
            /> function is already a loop &mdash; p5 calls it about sixty times
            a second, and animation is what that repetition looks
            like.
          </p>

          <dl>
            <dt>Frame</dt>
            <dd>One pass of draw(), producing one picture.</dd>
            <dt>Frame rate</dt>
            <dd>How many frames are drawn per second, around 60 by default.</dd>
            <dt>Global variable</dt>
            <dd>
            A variable declared outside every function, so it keeps its
            value between passes.
            </dd>
            <dt>Animation loop</dt>
            <dd>
            A loop that redraws a scene repeatedly to create movement.
            </dd>
          </dl>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section>
          <h2><span class="text-sn-theme">3.</span> Counting With for</h2>

          <p>
            When the number of passes is known ahead
            of time, a counted loop puts all three parts of the loop on one
            line.
          </p>

          <dl>
            <dt>Counted loop</dt>
            <dd>A loop that runs a known number of times.</dd>
            <dt>Loop counter</dt>
            <dd>
            The variable that tracks which pass the loop is on, usually
            called <CodeSnippet code="i" lang={"javascript"} theme={"material-theme-ocean"} inline />.
            </dd>
            <dt>Increment</dt>
            <dd>Adding one to a variable.</dd>
            <dt>Decrement</dt>
            <dd>Subtracting one from a variable.</dd>
          </dl>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section>
          <h2><span class="text-sn-theme">4.</span> Loop Patterns</h2>

          <p>
            Totals, counts, maximums, and averages are
            the same handful of shapes. What separates them is the starting
            value.
          </p>

          <dl>
            <dt>Counter</dt>
            <dd>A variable that counts how many times something happened.</dd>
            <dt>Running maximum</dt>
            <dd>The largest value seen so far.</dd>
            <dt>Initialization</dt>
            <dd>
            The starting value given to a variable before a loop, which
            decides whether the pattern works.
            </dd>
          </dl>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section>
          <h2><span class="text-sn-theme">5.</span> Loops Inside Loops</h2>

          <p>
            The inner loop finishes completely on
            every single pass of the outer one, which is why the total number
            of passes multiplies.
          </p>

          <dl>
            <dt>Nested loop</dt>
            <dd>A loop written inside another loop's body.</dd>
            <dt>Outer loop</dt>
            <dd>The loop that contains the other one.</dd>
            <dt>Inner loop</dt>
            <dd>The loop that runs completely on each outer pass.</dd>
            <dt>String accumulator</dt>
            <dd>A text variable built up piece by piece across a loop.</dd>
          </dl>
        </section>

        <hr />

        <section>
          <h2><span class="text-sn-theme">6.</span> p5 Lab 5: Grids</h2>

          <p>
            A grid is a nested loop with the two
            counters turned into coordinates.
          </p>

          <dl>
            <dt>Spacing</dt>
            <dd>The distance between neighboring items in a grid.</dd>
            <dt>Margin</dt>
            <dd>The offset that keeps a grid away from the canvas edge.</dd>
            <dt>
            <CodeSnippet code="noStroke()" lang={"javascript"} theme={"material-theme-ocean"} inline />
            </dt>
            <dd>Turns off shape outlines.</dd>
          </dl>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  dl {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  dt {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
  }
  dd {
    margin-bottom: 0;
    padding-left: 1rem;
  }
  section {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
  code {
    font-size: 1rem;
  }
</style>
